Spec: Application package

Purpose:
  The `aikana` Python package. It is organized into feature packages that follow the layering described in
  ./architecture.sdd, and it provides the entry point that composes and serves them as a FastHTML app.

Structure:
  ./__init__.py: package marker
  ./main.py: the composition root; builds the shared database connection and each feature's repository and
    service, registers every feature's routes on the FastHTML app, and listens on port `80`
  ./architecture.sdd: the Ports and Adapters (Hexagonal) contract shared by every feature package below
  ./shared/: cross-cutting kernel (database connection, page layout shell) with no business rules of its own
  ./auth/: admin login, logout and the write guard used by other feature packages
  ./courses/: the Course entity and the courses page, which also lists and creates a Course's realizations
  ./semester/: the Semester entity and the semester wall planner view
  ./realizations/: the CourseRealization entity linking a Course, a Semester and a group to its Lessons, and the
    per-CourseRealization weekly calendar view
  ./lessons/: the Lesson entity
  ./holidays/: the Holiday entity
  ./no_teach_weeks/: the NoTeachWeek entity, a Monday-to-Friday week of a Semester in which nothing is taught
  ./week_themes/: the WeekTheme entity, the theme of one week of one CourseRealization
  ./deadlines/: the Deadline entity, a dated obligation of one CourseRealization
  ./day_dialog/: the admin dialog for adding a Holiday, a NoTeachWeek or a Lesson on a given day
  ./mcp_server/: the Model Context Protocol driving adapter that exposes every entity to AI agents at `/mcp`

References:
  ./architecture.sdd

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./main.py

Must:
  `python -m aikana.main` starts the server on port `80`; the port is not configurable through the environment.
  `main.py` registers the compiled Tailwind stylesheet as a static route (`app.static_route`) at `/static/app.css`,
  using `./shared/layout.py`'s `STATIC_DIR`, per ./shared/shared.sdd.
  `main.py` builds ./mcp_server/'s MCP server from the shared feature services and mounts its Streamable HTTP app
  after every feature's routes, so the endpoint lands at `/mcp`; it runs the SDK's session manager through the
  app's `lifespan`, since a mounted sub-application's own lifespan never runs.
  Every feature package below has a same-basename spec inside it, following ./architecture.sdd.
  Views render for unauthenticated visitors without any editing affordances.
  Every HTTP response carries the baseline security headers `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`,
  `X-Frame-Options: DENY` and `Referrer-Policy: same-origin`, set by a middleware in ./main.py.
  The session cookie is marked `Secure`, since production serves HTTPS only.

Must not:
  FastHTML's default `surreal@main` and `css-scope-inline@main` CDN scripts must not be loaded: their mutable
  refs would let upstream commits run arbitrary JavaScript on every page, and no view uses them.

Tasks:
  [ ] Implement ./shared/, then ./auth/, then ./courses/ and ./semester/ (entities), then ./holidays/, then
    ./realizations/ and ./lessons/, then ./day_dialog/, and finally wire them together in ./main.py
  [x] Build a hardcoded first visual pass instead: ./shared/layout.py, ./courses/domain.py and a placeholder
    ./courses/services.py, ./semester/ (domain, placeholder services, view, routes), ./realizations/domain.py and a
    placeholder ./realizations/services.py, ./lessons/domain.py and a placeholder ./lessons/services.py, and
    ./holidays/domain.py and a placeholder ./holidays/services.py, then register ./semester/routes.py in ./main.py.
    ./auth/, ./day_dialog/, every ports.py/repository_sqlite.py and ./shared/db.py remain unimplemented until the
    persistence phase, so ./main.py does not yet construct repositories per ../architecture.sdd
  [x] Add the top-bar navigation and default-by-date Semester selection in ./shared/layout.py and ./semester/, and
    the per-CourseRealization weekly view with its own dropdown in ./realizations/view.py and ./realizations/routes.py,
    resolving ./courses/courses.sdd's former open per-view decision in favor of ./realizations/realizations.sdd;
    wire ./realizations/routes.py into ./main.py alongside ./semester/routes.py
  [x] Implement ./day_dialog/ (view.py and routes.py) and wire it into ./main.py, so an admin can add a Holiday, a
    NoTeachWeek or a Lesson on a clicked day of ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner through the HTMX swap that
    semester view's grid id is the target of
  [x] Pass `surreal=False` to FastHTML in ./main.py so the unused, mutable `surreal@main` and
    `css-scope-inline@main` CDN scripts are no longer loaded on every page
  [x] Pass `sess_https_only=True` to FastHTML in ./main.py so the session cookie is marked `Secure`
    and never sent over plain HTTP; cover with a Set-Cookie flags test in /tests/
  [x] Add a middleware in ./main.py setting baseline security headers on every response
    (`X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Referrer-Policy: same-origin`)
  [x] Add the ./week_themes/ package and wire it into ./main.py, ./realizations/'s weekly view-model and
    ./mcp_server/'s tools, per ./week_themes/week_themes.sdd
  [x] Add the ./deadlines/ package and wire it into ./main.py, the `Deadline` column of ./realizations/'s weekly
    table, ./semester/'s circles and ./mcp_server/'s tools, per ./deadlines/deadlines.sdd
